cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "unpool: recover individual-level data from publications that report only the pooled summary"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Canudo-Barreras
    given-names: Guillermo
    affiliation: Independent researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1949-9185"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gcanudo-barreras/unpool"
abstract: >-
  Agentic workflow that finds per-animal longitudinal series (tumour volume,
  bioluminescence, body weight) in the open-access supplementary spreadsheets
  of preclinical papers whose figures report only group means. A scanner
  proposes sheets on structure, an agent reads each against its figure legend
  and cuts it by treatment arm, a person verifies, and one command exports the
  campaign as a per-animal CSV with provenance and licence. Every performance
  figure was measured in a pre-registered study.
keywords:
  - individual participant data
  - preclinical
  - tumour growth
  - supplementary material
  - Europe PMC
  - data reuse
